    "result_text": "All tests pass. The full suite (which contains the single `AcceptanceTest`) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `customerCode` assignment for owners, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, keeping each piece of logic in the layer where it belongs:\n\n**Formatting logic** \u2014 new `util/CustomerCodeGenerator.java` (mirrors the existing `PersonNameFormatter`): `format(lastName, sequence)` \u2192 upper-cased first three letters of the last name + `-` + the 4-digit zero-padded sequence.\n\n**Persistence** \u2014 `customerCode` is derived from the owner count at creation time, so it must be stored:\n- `model/Owner.java`: added the `customerCode` field (`customer_code` column) with getter/setter.\n- Added the `customer_code` column to all four schema files (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 tests run on `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`.\n\n**Sequence source** \u2014 added `long count()` to the `OwnerRepository` interface and implemented it in all three profiles (Spring Data JPA via `@Query`, JPA, JDBC).\n\n**Assignment** \u2014 `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` now, only for new owners, sets `customerCode = CustomerCodeGenerator.format(lastName, count() + 1)`, alongside the existing new-owner handling (duplicate-telephone check, default registration date). Counting before the insert makes `NNNN` equal to one more than the current number of owners, so consecutive creates increment by exactly one.\n\n**Exposure** \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the OpenAPI `Owner` schema (next to `displayName`/`initials`). MapStruct maps it into `OwnerDto` automatically by name, so it appears in both the `POST` response and `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nThe acceptance test confirms `SMI-*` / `JON-*` prefixes and the +1 global sequence across two creates.",
